A vast ocean at twilight with dozens of ships from different eras and technologies—wooden sailing vessels, steam-powered boats, modern container ships, and futuristic hovercrafts—all attempting to communicate across the water using different signal methods: smoke signals, semaphore flags, radio antennas, and glowing holographic beams. Some ships successfully exchange signals while others drift past each other obliviously, their incompatible communication systems creating visible waves of interference patterns in the air. The scene is rendered in Piet Mondrian's distinctive style with bold primary colors of red, yellow, and blue divided by thick black lines, the ships and waves abstracted into geometric rectangular forms, the entire composition structured as an asymmetrical grid where the chaos of miscommunication meets rigid geometric order.
